   "id": "T1",
   "title": "A morning of ticks over five holdings",
   "why": "Frame 0 is the service's own figures. The newest valid tick of a symbol stands: a price of nothing leaves the last good one. A tick moves a row only when it is a WebSocket tick newer than the read: one stamped before the read, and one the REST fallback brought, change nothing. A tick with no previous close moves the price but keeps the service's close (and a row with none stays 'not known yet'). 10.125 is exactly 1012.5 paise and Python rounds that to 1012 (half to even), not 1013: the phone has to do the same. The fund has no tick.",
